Stop the frame thread waiting on the GPU when a draw batch fills. A batch
whose arenas or descriptor pool are full is submitted without a fence wait,
and recording continues into a second command buffer, fence, arena set,
descriptor pools and deferred-destroy list; that set is waited on only
when it comes round again. Every other flush (readback, present, release)
still waits, and drains the spare batch too. The descriptor pool holds
8192 sets (was 1024) so a busy frame fits one batch. In WKC2's town this
cut renderer blocking from about 31 ms to about 13 ms a frame.
RSX_VK_FLUSH_FILE=<path> writes, every five seconds, flushes per frame and
their time by source line (negative line = submitted without waiting).

